From: WikiReader emulator differential testing
Subject: [PATCH] [gcc] Fix fold discarding a narrowing cast in extract_muldiv

extract_muldiv_1 folds (T)(x * C1) * C2 into x * (C1 * C2), dropping the
conversion to T entirely, when T is a narrower signed type:

    u32 s;
    (u32)(signed char)(s * 0xdeadbeefu) * 3u

C requires the multiply, then truncation to signed char, then the second
multiply.  At -O1 and above gcc emits s * (0xdeadbeef * 3) with no
sign-extension instruction anywhere in the generated code.  It is not
merely a constant-folding fault: a volatile operand, which cannot be
folded, is miscompiled the same way.

The CONVERT_EXPR case guards against passing a multiply through a
truncating conversion with

    GET_MODE_SIZE (TYPE_MODE (ctype)) < GET_MODE_SIZE (TYPE_MODE (TREE_TYPE (op0)))

but ctype is not this node's type.  At the top of extract_muldiv_1,

    ctype = (wide_type != 0 && wider than type) ? wide_type : type;

and the CONVERT_EXPR case passes ctype down as the next wide_type.  So on
the inner conversion node type is signed char while ctype has become
unsigned int, both TYPE_MODE sizes in the test are 4, the comparison is
false, and the 8-bit narrowing is invisible.

Test TYPE, the type this conversion converts to, which is what the
"is this a truncation" question is actually about.  Widening conversions
are unaffected: for (long long)(int) the test is 8 < 4, still false.

Found by differential testing against a host compiler; the WikiReader
firmware itself does not trigger it (268 translation units compiled with
an instrumented compiler, zero sites reached).
---
 gcc/fold-const.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/fold-const.c b/gcc/fold-const.c
--- a/gcc/fold-const.c
+++ b/gcc/fold-const.c
@@ -4114,9 +4114,14 @@ extract_muldiv_1 (t, c, code, wide_type)
 	       && (GET_MODE_SIZE (TYPE_MODE (ctype))
 	           > GET_MODE_SIZE (TYPE_MODE (TREE_TYPE (op0)))))
-	      /* ... or its type is larger than ctype,
-		 then we cannot pass through this truncation.  */
-	      || (GET_MODE_SIZE (TYPE_MODE (ctype))
+	      /* ... or this is a truncation (t is narrower than op0),
+		 then we cannot pass through this narrowing.  Note this
+		 must test TYPE, the type this conversion converts *to*,
+		 not CTYPE: when a WIDE_TYPE has been propagated inwards
+		 CTYPE is that wider type, which hides the narrowing
+		 entirely.  Testing CTYPE lets (T)(x * C1) * C2 fold to
+		 x * (C1 * C2) with the conversion to T discarded.  */
+	      || (GET_MODE_SIZE (TYPE_MODE (type))
 		  < GET_MODE_SIZE (TYPE_MODE (TREE_TYPE (op0))))
 	      /* ... or signedness changes for division or modulus,
 		 then we cannot pass through this conversion.  */
